# Explain implementation (cursor-packs)

**CONSTRAINT:** When the agent finishes an implementation or fix that changed project files, or when the user asks what changed / how it was built, MUST Read and follow `.cursor/skills/explain-implementation/SKILL.md` before the final user-facing reply.

- MUST: short lead + scannable list or tiny diagram for how it fits together.
- MUST NOT: end with only a file list / “want me to commit?” and no explain.
- MUST NOT: ship a prose essay for the explain pass.
- Enforcement: Before send on an implement/fix turn, confirm the skill was applied to the reply draft.
- Violation: STOP, Read the skill, rewrite the reply, then send.

CORRECT:
```text
Lead line + 3–5 behavior bullets (optional mermaid)
```

PROHIBITED:
```text
Multi-paragraph walkthrough, or “Done. Tests pass. Commit?”
```

Chat voice remains `.cursor/rules/always-rules-01-human-interaction.mdc` outside this explain pass. This rule requires a scannable post-implementation explain.
